// Host-specific overrides for hestia (UTM/QEMU guest).
// No `output "Virtual-1"` block here on purpose — UTM's DynamicResolution
// + spice-vdagent re-advertise the preferred mode and a sensible scale
// as the UTM window is resized or moved between displays, and any static
// scale/mode setting would fight that. Use the Mod+- / Mod+= keybinds
// (defined in the shared niri config) to override scale on demand.

// Niri doesn't honor XDG autostart, so the per-user spice-vdagent client
// (needed for clipboard + dynamic resolution + cursor sync between host
// and guest) won't launch automatically the way it would under Plasma.
// Spawn it explicitly at session start.
spawn-at-startup "spice-vdagent"
